				    </apex:panelGrid>
					<apex:panelGrid cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
						<div class="Title" align="left">DCS Consultant Wins Top Honor in Prestigious Salesforce.com Contest
</div>
						<br/>
						<div align="left">
							<p><strong>MINNEAPOLIS, October 2009</strong>¿Demand Chain Systems¿a leading Twin Cities-based CRM consulting and implementation firm¿announced that one of its consultants was selected as a winner of the Force.com Sites Developer Challenge, a contest sponsored by salesforce.com.</p>
							<p>In the second-annual Challenge, salesforce.com encouraged developers to build new and exciting web applications with salesforce.com's new Force.com platform. Judges said they were looking for "style, technical ability, pizzazz and that little x-factor." </p>
							<p>Tim Inman, a senior technical analyst at DCS, displayed all three and was chosen as one of the top three winners of the challenge. Inman claimed the top prize with his enduranceAthlete, a Force.com application that plans, tracks and analyzes workouts, complete with video overviews.</p>
							<p>Inman is no stranger to success with the challenge: He was chosen as one of three honorable mentions in the first Developer Challenge in 2008.</p>
							<p><strong>About Demand Chain Systems</strong><br/>Demand Chain Systems (www.demandchainsystems.com) is a CRM consulting and implementation firm that mitigates the time, cost and disruption of transitioning to a new CRM system. The company quickly identifies high-value features to deliver first and stages implementations to match what clients can reasonably absorb. Demand Chain Systems is among the most experienced CRM teams in the Twin Cities and has helped hundreds of companies properly migrate from older CRM systems to newer on-demand systems, both locally and globally. </p>
						</div>
